From f7973ceeaaaa45fbe4beb80dfd761bde9fefcbc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 05:21:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make sandbox a fact about the provider, not the deployment
 posture
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`isSandboxProvider()` read:

    return providerId === 'mock' || this.rt.config.isSandbox

`sandbox: true` is the flag CostController.authorize() reads to decide NOT to
enforce. It gates five separate denials: the unknown-price denial, the
zero-price denial, `mode.sandbox_required` itself, the live-spend cap, and the
human-approval gate (controller.ts:104,114,128,198,219).

So in MASTERCLIP_MODE=sandbox — the default, and what render.yaml deploys, since
it never sets the variable — every real-provider request was stamped sandbox and
every rail was skipped. Sandbox mode disabled the guard rails instead of
refusing the work. Adding a provider key to the deployment would have spent real
money with nothing checking it, and the charge would have been written to the
ledger as sandbox = 1, so the cap would not have counted it afterwards either.

Two things let this survive a review aimed directly at it. The predicate was
private, so nothing could test it. And cost-engine's own
`blocks every billable submission while the mode is sandbox` hands the
controller `sandbox: false` by hand: it proves the gate works and never proves
anything reaches the gate. A green test that guards nothing is worse than no
test, because it answers the question.

The fix is the deletion. The predicate is now `isFreeProvider()`, exported so it
can be tested, and a pure function of the provider id.

Ported from the music-artist-hub copy of this tree, where it was committed as
9d0f814 while render.yaml still deployed masterclip from that directory. The
risk-register edits are the sandbox rows only; row 23 is left at the newer
wording this repository already had.
